    "key": "Fresh in-memory Ed25519 fixture key signed one V2 envelope per test. The public SPKI was admitted by the stock loopback attachment configuration. The bearer token was minted by the owned TLS/JWKS fixture.",
    "boundary": "HTTP 100 Continue was observed after the bearer pipeline and controller transport checks began the body read. The database baseline was read while the request was open. The client sent 642 of 1,285 envelope bytes and half-closed its write side. Bandit reported Unrecoverable error: closed for that exact POST before the complete body could reach the persistence path.",
    "persistence": "The same build record and revision-5 journal, exact unassigned OTA head, and zero release publications, OTA artifact rows or customer audit rows were observed pre-cut, post-cut, after HTTP 201 and after HTTP 200. The PostgreSQL attachment rows changed from zero to one only after the full authorized retry. The one row matched the full signed envelope, operation, revision, attempt, binding, public key and origin, and replay preserved its bytes.",
    "isolation": "Fresh per-attempt PostgreSQL clusters used only one owned Unix socket directory and no TCP bind. Phoenix and TLS used ephemeral loopback listeners. Dependencies were resolved offline from exact locally cached Hex packages into copied tool homes. No Xcode, device, external service, prior keys, product edits or shared service ran."
